    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48437",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "HOSTESS.\nPrithee, honey, sweet husband, let me bring thee to Staines.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48437/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48437/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 69,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1947866,
        "end": 1947949,
        "line": 72444,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@48437",
        "anchor": "sceneII_11.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "HOSTESS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "PISTOL.\nNo; for my manly heart doth yearn.\nBardolph, be blithe; Nym, rouse thy vaunting veins;\nBoy, bristle thy courage up; for Falstaff he is dead,\nAnd we must yearn therefore.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 7,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524/line-2",
          "start": 8,
          "end": 42,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524/line-3",
          "start": 43,
          "end": 94,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524/line-4",
          "start": 95,
          "end": 148,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48524/line-5",
          "start": 149,
          "end": 177,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1947953,
        "end": 1948159,
        "line": 72448,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@48524",
        "anchor": "sceneII_11.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "PISTOL.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 7
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48734",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "BARDOLPH.\nWould I were with him, wheresome’er he is, either in heaven or in hell!",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48734/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 9,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48734/line-2",
          "start": 10,
          "end": 81,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1948163,
        "end": 1948258,
        "line": 72455,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@48734",
        "anchor": "sceneII_11.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "BARDOLPH.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 9
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48833",
      "type": "speech",
      "tag": "p",
      "classes": [],
      "text": "HOSTESS.\nNay, sure, he’s not in hell. He’s in Arthur’s bosom, if ever man went to Arthur’s bosom. ’A made a finer end and went away an it had been any christom child. ’A parted even just between twelve and one, even at the turning o’ the tide: for after I saw him fumble with the sheets, and play with flowers, and smile upon his fingers’ ends, I knew there was but one way; for his nose was as sharp as a pen, and ’a babbled of green fields. “How now, Sir John!” quoth I; “what, man! be o’ good cheer.” So ’a cried out, “God, God, God!” three or four times. Now I, to comfort him, bid him ’a should not think of God; I hop’d there was no need to trouble himself with any such thoughts yet. So ’a bade me lay more clothes on his feet. I put my hand into the bed and felt them, and they were as cold as any stone. Then I felt to his knees, and so upward and upward, and all was as cold as any stone.",
      "separatorAfter": "\n\n",
      "spans": [],
      "lines": [
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48833/line-1",
          "start": 0,
          "end": 8,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        },
        {
          "id": "king-henry-the-fifth/sceneII_11.3/p@48833/line-2",
          "start": 9,
          "end": 898,
          "sourceLineNumber": null
        }
      ],
      "sourceRef": {
        "start": 1948262,
        "end": 1949186,
        "line": 72459,
        "column": 1,
        "path": "chap11/p@48833",
        "anchor": "sceneII_11.3"
      },
      "speakerLabel": "HOSTESS.",
      "attribution": {
        "status": "explicit",
        "cueStart": 0,
        "cueEnd": 8
      }
    },
